                    "Kotlin's `reversed()` answers a fresh list; this borrows and emits",
                    "projections like [iter] does, so `for x in reversed(xs)` costs nothing per",
                    "element. A caller wanting the reversed *list* writes `to_list(reversed(xs))`.",
